<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="a10-unit-008-excerpt"><section id="fs-id1170654889475">
<title>Evaluate an Expression</title>
<para id="fs-id1170654968998">In the last few examples, we simplified expressions using the order of operations. Now we’ll evaluate some expressions—again following the order of operations. To <emphasis effect="bold">evaluate an expression</emphasis> means to find the value of the expression when the variable is replaced by a given number.</para>
<note id="fs-id1170654969001">
<title>Evaluate an Expression</title>
<para id="fs-id1170655161751">To <term id="term-00018">evaluate an expression</term> means to find the value of the expression when the variable is replaced by a given number.</para>
</note>
<para id="fs-id1170655353204">To evaluate an expression, substitute that number for the variable in the expression and then simplify the expression.</para>
<example id="fs-id1170654889272">
<exercise id="fs-id1170654889274">
<problem id="fs-id1170655154711">
<para id="fs-id1170655154713">Evaluate <m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> when <span class="token">ⓐ</span> <m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <span class="token">ⓑ</span> <m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>.</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
</problem>
<solution id="fs-id1170655177952">
<title>Solution</title>
<para id="fs-id1166424830192"><span class="token">ⓐ</span> <newline/>
<table id="fs-id1167836329359" class="unnumbered unstyled" aria-label="The figure has two columns, with instructions on the left and math on the right. On the left, the text says “When x equals 5.” On the right is the expression 7x minus 4. One line down is the expression with 5 substituted for x: 7, open parenthesis, 5, close parenthesis, minus 4. One line down on the left, the instructions say “Multiply.” On the right is the expression 35 minus 4. One line down on the left, the instructions say “Subtract.” To the write is the number 31, which is the simplified expression."><label/><tgroup cols="2">
 <tbody>
  <row>
    <entry><media id="fs-id1167836295066" alt="The text 'when x = 5' is displayed against a white background, with the number 5 subtly highlighted in red."><image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/CNX_ElemAlg_Figure_01_02_009a_img_new.jpg"/></media></entry>
    <entry><media id="fs-id1167829597558" alt="A mathematical expression '7x-4' is shown on a white background, featuring the number 7, the variable x, a minus sign, and the number 4."><image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/CNX_ElemAlg_Figure_01_02_009b_img_new.jpg"/></media></entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry/>
    <entry><media id="fs-id1167833076771" alt="A mathematical expression showing 7 multiplied by 5, with 4 subtracted from the result, appearing as 7(5)-4. The number 5 is highlighted in red."><image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/CNX_ElemAlg_Figure_01_02_009c_img_new.jpg"/></media></entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry>Multiply.</entry>
    <entry><media id="fs-id1167836554298" alt="The image displays the numbers '35-4' in a dark gray font against a white background."><image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/CNX_ElemAlg_Figure_01_02_009d_img_new.jpg"/></media></entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry>Subtract.</entry>
    <entry><media id="fs-id1167836507263" alt="The number '31' is clearly visible in the top right corner of a plain white background."><image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/CNX_ElemAlg_Figure_01_02_009e_img_new.jpg"/></media></entry>
  </row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</para>
<para id="fs-id1167829683833"><span class="token">ⓑ</span> <newline/>
<table id="fs-id1167833047529" class="unnumbered unstyled" aria-label="The figure has two columns, with instructions on the left and math on the right. On the left, the text says “When x equals 1.” On the right is the expression 7x minus 4. One line down is the expression with 1 substituted for x: 7, open parenthesis, 1, close parenthesis, minus 4. One line down on the left, the instructions say “Multiply.” On the right is the expression 7 minus 4. One line down on the left, the instructions say “Subtract.” To the write is the number 3, which is the simplified expression."><label/><tgroup cols="2">
 <tbody>
  <row>
    <entry><media id="fs-id1167829597755" alt="The text 'when x = 1' is displayed on a white background, with '1' highlighted in red."><image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/CNX_ElemAlg_Figure_01_02_010a_img_new.jpg"/></media></entry>
    <entry><media id="fs-id1167836492302" alt="The mathematical expression '7x-4' is displayed on a white background, featuring the number 7, the variable x, a minus sign, and the number 4."><image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/CNX_ElemAlg_Figure_01_02_010b_img_new.jpg"/></media></entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry/>
    <entry><media id="fs-id1167836296392" alt="A mathematical expression reads '7(1)-4', with the number 1 prominently highlighted in red."><image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/CNX_ElemAlg_Figure_01_02_010c_img_new.jpg"/></media></entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry>Multiply.</entry>
    <entry><media id="fs-id1167836294733" alt="The numbers 7-4 are displayed on a white background, suggesting a score, date, or simple numerical notation."><image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/CNX_ElemAlg_Figure_01_02_010d_img_new.jpg"/></media></entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry>Subtract.</entry>
    <entry><media id="fs-id1167833014906" alt="A close-up of a large, dark grey numeral 3 on a clean white background."><image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/CNX_ElemAlg_Figure_01_02_010e_img_new.jpg"/></media></entry>
  </row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table></para>
</solution>
</exercise>
</example>
<note id="fs-id1170654936461" class="try">
<exercise id="fs-id1170654920156">
<problem id="fs-id1170654920158">
<para id="fs-id1170655196807">Evaluate <m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> when <span class="token">ⓐ</span> <m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <span class="token">ⓑ</span> <m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>.</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
</problem>
<solution id="fs-id1170654913926">
<para id="fs-id1170654913929"><span class="token">ⓐ</span> 13 <span class="token">ⓑ</span> 5</para>
</solution>
</exercise>
</note>
<note id="fs-id1170654968085" class="try">
<exercise id="fs-id1170654928390">
<problem id="fs-id1170654928392">
<para id="fs-id1170654928394">Evaluate <m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> when <span class="token">ⓐ</span> <m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <span class="token">ⓑ</span> <m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>.</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
</problem>
<solution id="fs-id1170654941204">
<para id="fs-id1170655068157"><span class="token">ⓐ</span> 8 <span class="token">ⓑ</span> 16</para>
</solution>
</exercise>
</note>
<example id="fs-id1170655213474">
<exercise id="fs-id1170655213476">
<problem id="fs-id1170655213478">
<para id="fs-id1170655129489">Evaluate the following for <m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> when <span class="token">ⓐ</span> <m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> <span class="token">ⓑ</span> <m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup><m:mo>.</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
</problem>
<solution id="fs-id1170654943583">
<title>Solution</title>
<para id="fs-id1166424780807"><span class="token">ⓐ</span> <newline/>
<table id="fs-id1167829717426" class="unnumbered unstyled" aria-label="The figure has two columns, with instructions on the left and math on the right. On the left, the text says “Replace x with 4.” On the right is the term x squared. One line down, the instructions on the left say “Use definition of exponent.” On the right is the term 4 squared. One line down on the left, the instructions say “Simplify.” On the right is the expression 4 times 4. Below this expression is the number 16, which is the result of substituting 4 for x."><label/><tgroup cols="2">
 <tbody>
  <row>
<entry/>
<entry align="center"><m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry><media id="fs-id1167826170152" alt="The image displays the text 'Replace x with 4.' in a gray sans-serif font, with the number 4 highlighted in red, on a plain white background."><image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/CNX_ElemAlg_Figure_01_02_011a_img_new.jpg"/></media></entry>
    <entry align="center"><media id="fs-id1167836526102" alt="A close-up image showing a large red number 4 raised to the power of 2."><image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/CNX_ElemAlg_Figure_01_02_011b_img_new.jpg"/></media></entry>
  </row>
  <row>
<entry>Use definition of exponent. </entry>
<entry align="center"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>·</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
  </row>
  <row>
<entry>Simplify.</entry>
<entry align="center"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>16</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
  </row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table></para>
<para id="fs-id1167836730046"><span class="token">ⓑ</span> <newline/>
<table id="fs-id1167836504155" class="unnumbered unstyled" aria-label="The figure has two columns, with instructions on the left and math on the right. On the left, the text says “Replace x with 4.” On the right is the term 3 to the 4th power. One line down, the instructions on the left say “Use definition of exponent.” On the right is the expression 3 times 3 times 3 times 3. One line down on the left, the instructions say “Simplify.” On the right is the number 81, which is the result of substituting 4 for x."><label/><tgroup cols="2">
 <tbody>
  <row>
<entry/>
<entry align="center"><m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mtext>x</m:mtext></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
  </row>
  <row>
    <entry><media id="fs-id1167829692365" alt="The text 'Replace x with 4.' is displayed in a digital format. The word 'Replace' and the letters 'x with' are in a dark gray font, while the number '4' is highlighted in a red-orange color, followed by a dark gray period. The background is white."><image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/CNX_ElemAlg_Figure_01_02_012a_img_new.jpg"/></media></entry>
    <entry align="center"><media id="fs-id1167836692989" alt="The mathematical expression showing 3 raised to the power of x, written as 3^x, where 3 is the base and x is the exponent."><image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/CNX_ElemAlg_Figure_01_02_012b_img_new.jpg"/></media></entry>
  </row>
  <row>
<entry>Use definition of exponent.</entry>
<entry align="center"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>·</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>·</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>·</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
  </row>
  <row>
<entry>Simplify.</entry>
<entry align="center"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>81</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
  </row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</para>
</solution>
</exercise>
</example>
<note id="fs-id1170655120535" class="try">
<exercise id="fs-id1170655120539">
<problem id="fs-id1170655202547">
<para id="fs-id1170655202549">Evaluate <m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> when <span class="token">ⓐ</span> <m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> <span class="token">ⓑ</span> <m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup><m:mo>.</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
</problem>
<solution id="fs-id1170654965432">
<para id="fs-id1170654931966"><span class="token">ⓐ</span> <m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>9</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <span class="token">ⓑ</span> <m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>64</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
</solution>
</exercise>
</note>
<note id="fs-id1170655353747" class="try">
<exercise id="fs-id1170655353751">
<problem id="fs-id1170655133647">
<para id="fs-id1170655133650">Evaluate <m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> when <span class="token">ⓐ</span> <m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> <span class="token">ⓑ</span> <m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup><m:mo>.</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
</problem>
<solution id="fs-id1170655126552">
<para id="fs-id1170654958705"><span class="token">ⓐ</span> <m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>216</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> <span class="token">ⓑ</span> <m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>64</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para>
</solution>
</exercise>
</note>
<example id="fs-id1170655171250">
<exercise id="fs-id1170655171252">
<problem id="fs-id1170655171254">
<para id="fs-id1170654957369">Evaluate <m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>.</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
</problem>
<solution id="fs-id1170655200587">
<title>Solution</title>
<para id="fs-id1169149281503"><table id="fs-id1169148881010" class="unnumbered unstyled" aria-label="The figure has two columns, with instructions on the left and math on the right. In the top right is the expression 2x squared plus 3x plus 8. One line down on the left, the text says “Substitute x equals 4.” On the right is the expression with 4 substituted for x: 2, open parenthesis, 4, close parenthesis, squared, plus 3, open parenthesis, 4, close parenthesis, plus 8. One line down, the instructions on the left say “Follow the order of operations.” On the right is the expression 2, open parenthesis, 16, close parenthesis, plus 3, open parenthesis, 4, close parenthesis, plus 8. Below this is the expression 32 plus 12 plus 8. Below this is 52, which is the result of substituting 4 for x in the expression.">
<label/>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colnum="1" colname="c1"/>
<colspec colnum="2" colname="c2"/>
<tbody>
<row valign="top">
<entry valign="top" align="left"/>
<entry align="center" valign="top"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
</row>
<row valign="top">
<entry valign="top" align="left"><media id="fs-id1169149357522" alt="The text 'Substitute x = 4.' is shown, with the number 4 highlighted in red."><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_ElemAlg_Figure_01_02_013a_img_new.jpg"/></media></entry>
<entry align="center" valign="top"><media id="fs-id1169149089480" alt="A mathematical expression reads 2x squared plus 3x plus 8, in a black font on a white background."><image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/CNX_ElemAlg_Figure_01_02_013b_img_new.jpg"/></media></entry>
</row>
<row valign="top">
<entry valign="top" align="left">Follow the order of operations.</entry>
<entry align="center" valign="top"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>(</m:mo><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:mo>)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
</row>
<row valign="top">
<entry valign="top" align="left"/>
<entry align="center" valign="top"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>32</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>12</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
</row>
<row valign="top">
<entry valign="top" align="left"/>
<entry align="center" valign="top"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>52</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table></para>
</solution>
</exercise>
</example>
<note id="fs-id1170655160606" class="try">
<exercise id="fs-id1170655160609">
<problem id="fs-id1170654942304">
<para id="fs-id1170654942306">Evaluate <m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>.</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
</problem>
<solution id="fs-id1170655209422">
<para id="fs-id1170655209424">40</para>
</solution>
</exercise>
</note>
<note id="fs-id1170655197213" class="try">
<exercise id="fs-id1170655197217">
<problem id="fs-id1170655163499">
<para id="fs-id1170655163501">Evaluate <m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>6</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> when <m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>.</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></para>
</problem>
<solution id="fs-id1170655106382">
<para id="fs-id1170655106384">9</para>
</solution>
</exercise>
</note>
</section>
</document>
